"# Farmgenie Fresh Cart (FFC)\n\nOffline Flutter Material 3 employee UI demonstration.\n\n## Current UI\n- Official Farmgenie logo on the Android launcher, Android startup screen, and Flutter splash. The original logo files are unchanged. The Flutter splash shows a loading indicator for 2.8 seconds; total cold-start time also depends on device/OS startup.\n- Validated mock login, username-only Remember Me, profile, logout confirmation, and authenticated navigation.\n- Side menu: Home, Attendance, Leave Request, Material Request, Shift Roster, Tasks & Handover, Inventory, Barcode Scanner, Stock Audit, Store Operations, Announcements, Help & Support, Profile.\n- Home: sample shift, check-in time, working hours excluding breaks, break duration, check-out status, priorities, notices, employee details, and quick actions.\n- Attendance: month navigation, date selection, present/absent/leave/weekly-off codes, future dates with no record, monthly totals, and selected-date hours. Status is communicated by text as well as color.\n- Leave Request: leave type, date range, required reason, and local request history.\n- Material Request: item, positive whole-number quantity, purpose, and local request history.\n- Roster, tasks, announcements, and support are previews. Inventory, barcode, stock audit, and operational processing remain Coming Soon.\n\n## Demo behavior and boundaries\nEnter any nonblank username and password. This is not real authentication or a security boundary. Remember Me retains only the username in memory during this app process, including after logout. Passwords are cleared on login and never persisted.\n\nAll employee and attendance data is fictional. Today's record is explicitly a sample snapshot at 14:00: check-in 09:02, 30-minute break, 4h 28m worked, no check-out. It is not a live clock or actual punch record. Past samples use deterministic statuses; future dates remain unrecorded.\n\nLeave and material forms save only to the current authenticated session. They do not send requests, approve leave, change calendar records, move stock, or notify anyone. Logout clears these demo requests. Canceling logout preserves the screen/session.\n\nThere is no ERPNext/API integration, geofencing, location permission, actual check-in/out, camera, database, attendance processing, or POS. These are a future phase, not included in this UI build.\n\n## Structure\n- lib/theme: centralized branding and Material 3 theme\n- lib/widgets: reusable layout, logo, cards, buttons, fields, and workday widgets\n- lib/models: employee, attendance status/day records, demo requests\n- lib/services: isolated mock session and workday controllers\n- lib/screens: separate screens and the drawer/bottom-navigation shell\n- assets/images/farmgenie_logo.png: unchanged official logo\n- android/app/src/main/res: official-logo launcher and native splash resources\n- test: session, login/logout, navigation, splash duration, calendar/leap-month handling, request validation/submission, and small-screen/large-text tests\n- tool/preview_test.dart: optional widget preview generator; standard Flutter test fonts are placeholders, so use device screenshots for typography review\n\nThe app uses only Flutter SDK runtime features. Replace the mock service layer with authenticated API services in the next phase, with server-authoritative attendance and explicit permission handling for geofencing.\n\n"
